1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:03,000
All right, the next section in the text, ovarian tumors.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:04,580
Before we can begin this discussion,

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:06,280
we've got to understand a little bit of normal,

4
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:07,440
so let's go to the whiteboard.

5
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:10,100
Remind ourselves that this is the ovary,

6
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:13,260
that the ovary histologically contains three major compartments.

7
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:15,540
It contains the oocyte, or the egg,

8
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:19,060
and from this oocyte, or egg, we can derive germ cell tumors.

9
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:22,180
It contains the cells that support the oocyte,

10
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:25,040
for example, the granulosa cells, the theca cells,

11
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:28,140
and the fibroblasts, which are the stromal cells

12
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:30,280
that are the connective tissue of the ovary,

13
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:35,300
and that entire category is called the sex cord stroma,

14
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:38,720
and so from that, we can derive sex cord stromal tumors,

15
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:42,220
and then the third possibility is that the ovary

16
00:00:42,220 --> 00:00:43,880
is lined by surface epithelium.

17
00:00:44,060 --> 00:00:47,140
The entire surface of the ovary has surface epithelium,

18
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:49,880
and from this surface epithelium, we can derive tumors,

19
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,340
and those are called surface epithelial tumors.

20
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:54,340
So once you understand this normal,

21
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:57,000
then you understand that there are three major categories

22
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,180
of ovarian tumors.

23
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:00,980
Now there's a fourth possibility, which would be metastasis.

24
00:01:01,480 --> 00:01:05,220
However, metastasis is going to be put off

25
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:06,740
until the very end of this discussion,

26
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:08,140
and we'll just discuss for now

27
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:11,680
the three categories of primary tumors of the ovary.

28
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:13,980
Now what I say here in your text

29
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:15,720
is that the ovary has three cell types.

30
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:18,100
Of course, it's surface epithelium, germ cells,

31
00:01:18,220 --> 00:01:19,420
and sex cord stroma,

32
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:21,880
and tumor can arise from any of these cell types

33
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:24,200
or from metastasis, which again we'll discuss

34
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:25,780
at the very end of this section.

35
00:01:26,580 --> 00:01:28,500
We'll start with the surface epithelial tumors

36
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:31,180
because they are the most common type of ovarian tumor,

37
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:32,880
and what I'd like to remind you

38
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:36,400
is that the surface epithelium of the ovary,

39
00:01:36,540 --> 00:01:38,180
the surface lining of the ovary,

40
00:01:38,180 --> 00:01:40,900
is also known as celomic epithelium.

41
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:43,100
Now this epithelium has the ability

42
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:45,100
to produce multiple different cell types,

43
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:46,260
just as the gyne tract

44
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:47,820
has multiple different cell types.

45
00:01:47,820 --> 00:01:49,280
For example, you're well aware

46
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:51,980
that the fallopian tube is normally lined by serous cells,

47
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:55,260
and that the endometrium is normally lined

48
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:56,980
by endometrial type cells,

49
00:01:57,080 --> 00:02:00,120
and that the endocervix is lined by mucinous type cells.

50
00:02:00,580 --> 00:02:04,840
And so this celomic epithelium that lines the ovary

51
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:06,880
also has the ability to produce

52
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:08,240
multiple different cell types.

53
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:10,000
And there's four different cell types

54
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:10,920
that we're gonna talk about,

55
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:12,920
but we're gonna start with the two most common.

56
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:14,800
The two most common cell types

57
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:17,420
that can arise with surface epithelial tumors

58
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:20,980
are serous tumors and mucinous tumors.

59
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:23,560
Now the way you wanna think about these

60
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,440
is that serous tumors and mucinous tumors

61
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:26,860
are usually cystic,

62
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:28,480
so that would be principle number one,

63
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:31,020
and that they are classically named

64
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:35,120
based on the type of fluid that they would produce.

65
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:36,960
So you'd have this big cystic tumor,

66
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:39,160
and if it was full of water when you cut it open,

67
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:40,700
we would call that a serous tumor.

68
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:43,660
And if it was full of mucus when you cut it open,

69
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:46,300
we would call that a mucinous tumor.

70
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:49,520
And this is the way that we classically named these tumors.

71
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:51,000
Now we can look under the microscope

72
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,720
and we can confirm whether the cells

73
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:54,040
are really serous or mucinous,

74
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:57,180
but that's a very sort of introductory way

75
00:02:57,180 --> 00:02:58,220
to look at these tumors.

76
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:00,820
So the two most common tumors of the surface

77
00:03:00,820 --> 00:03:02,740
are serous tumors and mucinous tumors.

78
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,140
Both are usually cystic.

79
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,680
When you have a serous tumor, it's usually full of water.

80
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:08,240
When you have a mucinous tumor,

81
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,600
it's usually full of mucus.

82
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:12,900
Now in addition, when you have surface epithelial tumors,

83
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:16,440
you can categorize those tumors based on how they behave.

84
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:19,680
So there are benign tumors, there are malignant tumors,

85
00:03:19,820 --> 00:03:21,360
and then there are tumors in between,

86
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:23,100
which are called borderline tumors.

87
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:26,840
Now the benign tumors are called cyst adenoma.

88
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:29,700
In particular, when we're dealing with the serous

89
00:03:29,700 --> 00:03:30,780
and the mucinous types,

90
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:33,100
they're going to be called cyst adenoma.

91
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:35,120
And that's because I told you that the serous tumors

92
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,860
make watery fluid producing a cyst,

93
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:40,360
and the mucinous tumors make mucousy fluid producing a cyst.

94
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:43,620
So if it's benign, it'll be called cyst because it's cystic,

95
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:46,100
and adeno because it's glandular cells,

96
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:47,980
and then oma because it's a benign mass.

97
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:49,660
So cyst adenoma.

98
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:53,140
Now the way by which we recognize a cyst adenoma

99
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:55,280
is that when you look at it on gross examination,

100
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:58,360
it is a single simple cyst,

101
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:00,200
and were you to look under the microscope,

102
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:03,580
you would see a simple flat lining to that cyst.

103
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:07,040
And so that's the classic feature of a cyst adenoma.

104
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:11,120
Now most commonly, these tumors arise in premenopausal women,

105
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:13,660
classically around the age of 30 to 40.

106
00:04:14,060 --> 00:04:15,960
And that's going to be important as we move forward.

107
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:18,280
So here's what a cyst adenoma looks like.

108
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:19,760
This is the cyst opened up,

109
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:22,460
and this is sort of half of it and the other half of it.

110
00:04:22,740 --> 00:04:24,100
And you can imagine, let's pretend,

111
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:25,720
if that was full of watery fluid

112
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:28,840
and the cells looked serous under the microscope,

113
00:04:28,980 --> 00:04:32,160
we would call that a serous cyst adenoma.

114
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:34,040
If it was full of mucousy fluid

115
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:36,240
and the cells looked mucinous under the microscope,

116
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:39,740
we would call that a mucinous cyst adenoma.

117
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:41,240
Again, both are benign.

118
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:45,200
Both would be seen around the age of 30 to 40 years of age.

119
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:48,280
The only other thing that I would like to say here

120
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:52,160
is that the way by which we can prove that they're benign

121
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:53,320
is when we look under the microscope,

122
00:04:53,620 --> 00:04:55,800
we would see that the entire cyst was lined

123
00:04:55,800 --> 00:05:00,120
by just a simple single layer of epithelial cells.

124
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:05,320
Now, in the malignant variant, we call that cyst adenocarcinoma.

125
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:07,120
Cyst because it's cystic,

126
00:05:07,740 --> 00:05:09,660
adeno because the cells are glandular,

127
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:13,900
and then carcinoma because it's a malignant epithelial tumor,

128
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:15,920
so cyst adenocarcinoma.

129
00:05:16,540 --> 00:05:18,520
Now, again, when you have a cyst adenocarcinoma,

130
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:20,140
you're going to have a large tumor,

131
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:21,440
and when you cut it open,

132
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:24,120
rather than having a simple single cyst,

133
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:27,900
you're going to have very complicated cysts, multiple cysts,

134
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:29,440
and then when you look at the lining,

135
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:32,180
instead of having that nice, smooth, shiny lining,

136
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:35,260
you'll actually see a shaggy lining, almost like a carpet,

137
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:38,600
and so that's the classic features of the malignant tumor.

138
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:40,380
Now, again, if it's a big cystic lesion

139
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:42,020
and you cut into it and water comes out,

140
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:45,220
you think about cirrus cyst adenocarcinoma,

141
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:47,420
and if it's a big tumor, cystic tumor,

142
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:50,020
and you cut it open and mucinous fluid comes out

143
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:51,300
or mucous fluid comes out,

144
00:05:51,540 --> 00:05:53,860
then you think about a mucinous cyst adenocarcinoma.

145
00:05:53,940 --> 00:05:56,420
You can confirm that by looking at the histology

146
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:58,000
to see whether the cells look cirrus

147
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,580
or whether they look mucinous,

148
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:01,120
but the key feature here, again,

149
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:04,000
is complex cysts with thick, shaggy lining.

150
00:06:04,580 --> 00:06:08,040
Now, of course, the defining feature of this malignancy

151
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:09,900
would be that the cells invade

152
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:13,540
into the connective tissue of the cyst wall,

153
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:15,900
so you'd have clear invasion of cells

154
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:17,820
into the connective tissue,

155
00:06:18,020 --> 00:06:20,000
which would then define that tumor

156
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,620
to be absolutely malignant.

157
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:24,680
Now, this commonly arises in postmenopausal women.

158
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:28,320
For example, the average age would be about 65 years of age.

159
00:06:28,940 --> 00:06:31,600
There is a third category for surface epithelial tumors,

160
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:33,240
and those are called borderline tumors.

161
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:35,520
The only thing you have to know about borderline tumors

162
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:38,560
is that they have features in between benign and malignant.

163
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:40,720
They are malignant.

164
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:42,880
They have metastatic potential.

165
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:45,380
However, they behave much better

166
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:47,120
than the clear-cut malignant tumors,

167
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:49,420
and so because they're sort of in between,

168
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:51,800
we call them borderline tumors.

169
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:54,580
Again, it's important to note that they have a better prognosis,

170
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:58,400
but they still carry metastatic potential

171
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:00,360
in that they are still malignant.

172
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:02,860
Now, one important association here

173
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:04,500
that's high yield for examinations,

174
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:05,900
especially board examinations,

175
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:08,160
is the fact that BRCA mutation carriers

176
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:11,180
can get a specific type of ovarian carcinoma.

177
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,100
Let's go back and remind ourselves

178
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:14,760
that patients who have BRCA1 mutations,

179
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:16,460
they have an increased risk of breast cancer,

180
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:17,820
but in addition to that,

181
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:20,340
they also have an increased risk of ovarian cancer.

182
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:24,680
It's not enough to know just that.

183
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:25,960
You need to go one step further

184
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:28,800
and know that the most classic type of tumor

185
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:31,720
that arises in the ovary in these patients

186
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:33,720
is a serous carcinoma.

187
00:07:33,860 --> 00:07:36,120
So these patients would get a surface epithelial tumor

188
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,260
that was malignant,

189
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:39,700
and it would be of the serous subtype.

190
00:07:40,260 --> 00:07:41,340
So that's important to know

191
00:07:41,340 --> 00:07:43,600
concerning BRCA1 mutation carriers.

192
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:45,560
The second important thing to know about these patients

193
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:48,140
is that not only do they have an increased risk of ovary,

194
00:07:48,140 --> 00:07:50,940
but they also have an increased risk of serous carcinoma

195
00:07:50,940 --> 00:07:52,080
of the fallopian tube.

196
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:54,100
And of course, that has clinical implications

197
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:56,360
because when patients have a BRCA mutation,

198
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:59,220
they may elect to, for example, remove both breasts

199
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:00,820
to reduce the risk of breast cancer.

200
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:03,840
And they may also elect to remove the ovary

201
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:05,000
and the fallopian tube,

202
00:08:05,260 --> 00:08:07,780
and they would have to remove the fallopian tube

203
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:11,640
to remove the risk of fallopian tube serous carcinoma as well.

204
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:16,280
And so that is an important clinical principle,

205
00:08:16,580 --> 00:08:19,120
and so therefore it becomes high yield for examinations.

206
00:08:19,660 --> 00:08:21,200
Now, I've only told you about two

207
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:22,640
of the surface epithelial tumors,

208
00:08:22,740 --> 00:08:24,300
which is that you can have serous tumors

209
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:25,660
or you can have mucinous tumors.

210
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:27,380
There are two other types

211
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:29,420
that are relatively high yield for exam.

212
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:33,280
The first is endometrioid surface tumors.

213
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:35,800
So we can have a surface epithelial tumor

214
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:38,240
that has endometrioid histology.

215
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,000
What do we mean by endometrioid?

216
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,860
We mean that it looks like endometrial cells.

217
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:44,540
So that's one possibility.

218
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:48,560
Now, a few things to know about endometrioid tumors

219
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:50,320
of the surface of the ovary.

220
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:52,460
The first point is that they're usually malignant.

221
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,200
Remember that surface epithelial tumors

222
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:56,260
can be benign, borderline, or malignant.

223
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:58,320
When you have an endometrioid tumor,

224
00:08:58,440 --> 00:08:59,400
it's usually malignant.

225
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:01,560
So you're going to have an endometrioid carcinoma.

226
00:09:01,660 --> 00:09:02,320
That's point one.

227
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:04,580
Point number two is that it usually arises,

228
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:06,060
or I shouldn't say usually,

229
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:08,880
but it may be associated with endometriosis.

230
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:11,960
This goes back to the discussion that we had

231
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,360
when we talked about endometriosis.

232
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:15,380
If you review your notes there,

233
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:17,880
you'll see that I said that in endometriosis,

234
00:09:18,020 --> 00:09:20,420
one of the complications was that carcinoma

235
00:09:20,420 --> 00:09:23,580
could develop particularly in the ovary.

236
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:27,780
And so there's an association of endometrioid carcinoma

237
00:09:27,780 --> 00:09:29,420
with endometriosis.

238
00:09:29,940 --> 00:09:31,800
And then the other important association

239
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:35,380
is that when patients have endometrioid carcinoma,

240
00:09:35,380 --> 00:09:38,080
15% of those patients will actually have

241
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:40,760
a separate endometrioid carcinoma

242
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:42,580
in the endometrium as well.

243
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:46,440
So 15% of patients with endometrioid carcinoma

244
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:48,500
of the ovary will also have

245
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:50,920
a separate endometrioid carcinoma

246
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:52,120
in the endometrium.

247
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:53,620
And so when we have patients

248
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:55,660
with endometrioid carcinoma of the ovary,

249
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:58,200
it's important to know, especially for exams,

250
00:09:58,540 --> 00:10:00,060
that we also need to look

251
00:10:00,060 --> 00:10:01,980
and see what's going on in their endometrium.

252
00:10:02,100 --> 00:10:03,840
There may be a cancer there as well.

253
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:06,980
The fourth type of surface epithelial tumor

254
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:08,320
is called a Brenner tumor.

255
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:10,480
The only thing for examination purposes

256
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:14,220
is that the Brenner tumor usually contains urothelium

257
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:15,960
as its type of epithelium.

258
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:18,300
So if you've got an ovarian tumor

259
00:10:18,300 --> 00:10:20,520
and they tell you that the ovarian tumor

260
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:23,200
contains cells that mimic the,

261
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:26,140
or that resemble urothelium,

262
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:28,300
then we would call that a Brenner tumor.

263
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:30,120
And that is a high yield principle

264
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:31,440
to be aware of as well.

265
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:33,020
Now, generally speaking,

266
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:35,160
when we talk about the surface epithelial tumors,

267
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:37,200
it's important to know that they present late.

268
00:10:37,860 --> 00:10:40,660
And that's going to result in a poor prognosis.

269
00:10:41,060 --> 00:10:44,000
Remember, the general principle in neoplasia

270
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,360
is that the longer the tumor can grow in the patient,

271
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:47,760
the more it can pick up mutations.

272
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:49,340
The more it picks up mutations,

273
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:50,540
the more it's going to be,

274
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:53,700
the more malignant it's going to become over time.

275
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:55,560
The surface epithelial tumors,

276
00:10:55,940 --> 00:10:57,360
there's a lot of room in the pelvis

277
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:58,480
for the ovary to grow,

278
00:10:58,480 --> 00:11:00,240
and so these tumors present late.

279
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:03,000
Now, they present with also very vague symptoms.

280
00:11:03,140 --> 00:11:05,620
For example, abdominal pain or fullness,

281
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:08,820
signs of compression with urinary frequency, et cetera.

282
00:11:09,560 --> 00:11:11,360
One of the mechanisms by which

283
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:14,000
ovarian epithelial tumors spread

284
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,220
is locally,

285
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:17,940
and they like to extend to involve the peritoneum.

286
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:20,540
Remember that we talked about three mechanisms of spread

287
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:21,760
in our neoplasia lecture,

288
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:24,880
and we said that carcinomas like to go to lymphatics.

289
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:29,460
The sarcomas like to go hematogenously and then spread,

290
00:11:29,740 --> 00:11:31,080
and then we mentioned at that point

291
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:33,320
that the ovary liked to spread locally

292
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:34,820
and involve the peritoneum.

293
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:36,080
And in particular,

294
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:37,400
I showed you a picture there

295
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:41,100
of a patient who had massive involvement of the omentum,

296
00:11:41,160 --> 00:11:43,140
and I told you that were you to cut through that,

297
00:11:43,220 --> 00:11:45,840
you would see something called omental caking.

298
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:47,680
And so when you cut through it,

299
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:48,820
it kind of looks like cake.

300
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:50,980
So they call that omental caking,

301
00:11:51,100 --> 00:11:53,800
and that's a high-yield thing to be aware of,

302
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:55,300
as I've already mentioned previously.

303
00:11:56,040 --> 00:11:57,500
The surface epithelial tumors,

304
00:11:57,640 --> 00:11:59,400
one of the interesting things

305
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:02,480
that they may release into the serum is CA-125.

306
00:12:03,340 --> 00:12:06,040
CA-125 is a serum tumor marker.

307
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:08,300
Remember that serum tumor markers,

308
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:09,060
generally speaking,

309
00:12:09,060 --> 00:12:11,620
can provide three separate benefits.

310
00:12:11,780 --> 00:12:12,980
They can be used for screening.

311
00:12:13,380 --> 00:12:14,980
They can be used to monitor treatment,

312
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:15,980
response,

313
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:18,280
and they can also be used to monitor recurrence.

314
00:12:18,740 --> 00:12:19,840
In the case of screening,

315
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:22,560
CA-125 is not really panned out to be useful.

316
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:25,000
However, in the case of monitoring treatment

317
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,480
and recurrence, it has.

318
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:27,640
So for example,

319
00:12:27,740 --> 00:12:30,460
if a patient has a surface epithelial tumor

320
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:32,460
and the CA-125 is high,

321
00:12:32,740 --> 00:12:34,060
once it's removed surgically,

322
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:36,440
the CA-125 should again go down

323
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:38,040
and should decrease to zero.

324
00:12:38,180 --> 00:12:39,980
So that's one important way

325
00:12:39,980 --> 00:12:41,560
by which we could use the CA-125.

326
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:43,320
And another important way

327
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:44,920
by which we could use the CA-125

328
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:46,320
is to screen for recurrence.

329
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:47,960
So let's say that a woman comes in,

330
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:51,700
she's got a history of serous carcinoma of the ovary,

331
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:53,280
and at the time of diagnosis,

332
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:54,860
her CA-125 was high.

333
00:12:55,420 --> 00:12:56,620
Now she comes in,

334
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:58,040
I don't know,

335
00:12:58,080 --> 00:12:59,800
a year later after surgical removal,

336
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:01,300
and she's having symptoms

337
00:13:01,300 --> 00:13:03,620
that suggest that there's recurrence of the tumor,

338
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:05,540
and a CA-125 is measured,

339
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:06,460
and it's high again.

340
00:13:06,460 --> 00:13:08,860
And that would be a pretty good indication

341
00:13:08,860 --> 00:13:10,560
that the patient now has recurrence.

342
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:12,300
So that would be something to consider

343
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:13,920
concerning CA-125.

344
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:18,060
The second category of tumors

345
00:13:18,060 --> 00:13:19,480
that can arise in the ovary

346
00:13:19,480 --> 00:13:20,820
are called the germ cell tumors.

347
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:24,100
This is the second most common ovarian tumor.

348
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:26,480
It's seen in 15% of the cases.

349
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:28,600
So of all of the ovarian tumors,

350
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:30,680
15% of cases are germ cell tumors.

351
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:32,980
Usually occurs in women of reproductive age.

352
00:13:32,980 --> 00:13:35,220
This is important because it allows us

353
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:36,880
to make a distinction clinically

354
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:38,420
and on examinations

355
00:13:38,420 --> 00:13:40,600
of what we're actually considering

356
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:42,080
when we deal with a particular patient.

357
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:42,920
So for example,

358
00:13:43,360 --> 00:13:44,480
if you're dealing with a woman

359
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:47,380
who's about the age of 15 to 30,

360
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:50,280
then I would think about a germ cell tumor.

361
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:52,060
So that would be high on my differential.

362
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:55,160
If I'm dealing with a woman that's 35 or 40,

363
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:58,460
I'm thinking of a benign surface epithelial tumor.

364
00:13:58,840 --> 00:14:00,360
And if I'm dealing with a woman

365
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:02,720
that's, for example, 60 or 70,

366
00:14:03,220 --> 00:14:05,240
my differential diagnosis at the top

367
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:07,740
is a malignant surface epithelial tumor.

368
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:09,640
So again, the age becomes important

369
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:11,760
when you look at a clinical vignette, for example.

370
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:14,000
Now the germ cell tumors,

371
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:17,840
a lot of students are sort of terrified

372
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:18,720
of these tumors

373
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:20,620
because it's hard to remember the types

374
00:14:20,620 --> 00:14:21,880
and exactly what's going on.

375
00:14:22,060 --> 00:14:23,580
But I actually think it's relatively easy

376
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:24,680
if you just remember

377
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:26,940
what the normal germ cell can make.

378
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:28,540
And based on what it can make,

379
00:14:28,620 --> 00:14:29,740
you can then subsequently

380
00:14:29,740 --> 00:14:31,780
sort of put the pieces together

381
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:33,620
and know the different tumors that can form.

382
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,920
For example, I'll show you how I do this.

383
00:14:36,220 --> 00:14:37,420
So when I think about the germ cell,

384
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:38,840
I remind myself that the germ cell

385
00:14:38,840 --> 00:14:40,460
can make fetal tissues, correct?

386
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:41,740
It's going to be able to make baby.

387
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:44,700
And so when it's going to make fetal-type tissues,

388
00:14:44,860 --> 00:14:46,880
one tumor that would resemble fetal tissues

389
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:49,080
would be something called a cystic teratoma.

390
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:52,520
So a cystic teratoma is, again,

391
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:57,160
a tumor that contains different embryologic layers.

392
00:14:57,400 --> 00:15:00,060
For example, it contains skin and teeth

393
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:01,960
and bone and hair and gut

394
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:04,040
and thyroid tissue, et cetera.

395
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:05,940
And so that's one example.

396
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:07,880
So we call that a cystic teratoma.

397
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:11,260
All right.

398
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:13,940
You can also get fetal-type tissue

399
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:16,080
that's very primitive in a germ cell tumor.

400
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:19,700
And we call that embryonal carcinoma.

401
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:22,280
Embryonal, i.e. embryo-like,

402
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:23,440
so that when you look at the cells

403
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,160
under the microscope,

404
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:25,240
they look very primitive,

405
00:15:25,440 --> 00:15:28,920
almost like the embryo-like cells.

406
00:15:29,340 --> 00:15:30,680
So that's embryonal carcinoma.

407
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:32,700
Another important type of tissue

408
00:15:32,700 --> 00:15:35,080
that the germ cell is going to make,

409
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:36,300
it's going to make the yolk sac.

410
00:15:36,900 --> 00:15:39,040
And so from that type of tissue,

411
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:41,320
we can have something called a yolk sac tumor.

412
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:44,940
Another type of tissue that the germ cell can make,

413
00:15:44,940 --> 00:15:46,840
it can make additional germ cells.

414
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:50,420
And when you have a tumor of a mass

415
00:15:50,420 --> 00:15:51,760
of a bunch of germ cells,

416
00:15:52,040 --> 00:15:53,640
we call that dysgerminoma.

417
00:15:59,930 --> 00:16:00,950
All right, dysgerminoma.

418
00:16:01,230 --> 00:16:02,310
And then in addition,

419
00:16:02,990 --> 00:16:05,110
the oocyte or the egg

420
00:16:05,110 --> 00:16:06,630
needs to be able to make placenta.

421
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:11,940
And so we can have a tumor of placental tissue,

422
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:14,140
and that's called choriocarcinoma.

423
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:16,460
And all of this basically summarizes

424
00:16:16,460 --> 00:16:18,600
the different types of germ cell tumors.

425
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:21,820
So there are five key germ cell tumors

426
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:22,560
to be aware of,

427
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:24,840
and all of them are explained here.

428
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:27,260
And now I'm going to walk you through them one by one.

429
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:29,180
So the first of these germ cell tumors

430
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:30,760
is a cystic teratoma.

431
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:32,560
Again, what is a cystic teratoma?

432
00:16:32,660 --> 00:16:34,860
It's a cystic tumor, hence the term cystic,

433
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:37,400
that's comprised of fetal tissue,

434
00:16:37,820 --> 00:16:41,600
and that is derived from two or three embryonic layers

435
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:42,880
or embryologic layers.

436
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:46,200
It's the most common germ cell tumor in females,

437
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:49,520
and 10% of the time, these tumors can be bilateral.

438
00:16:49,680 --> 00:16:51,080
So it would not be uncommon,

439
00:16:51,280 --> 00:16:52,220
even on an examination,

440
00:16:52,560 --> 00:16:55,180
to have a tumor on both the right side

441
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:58,180
and the left side in a particular patient.

442
00:16:58,780 --> 00:17:01,160
This is what the cystic teratoma looks like.

443
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:02,560
Basically, it's a tumor, again,

444
00:17:02,680 --> 00:17:07,100
composed of hair, teeth, bone, gut, thyroid,

445
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:09,940
basically any normal tissue

446
00:17:09,940 --> 00:17:11,960
that could be seen in a fetus.

447
00:17:12,380 --> 00:17:13,560
It's a cystic tumor.

448
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:15,220
This cyst here has been opened,

449
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:17,520
and we can see that this is full of hair.

450
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:19,660
Now, there's probably a tooth over here

451
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:20,760
or maybe a piece of bone,

452
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:22,400
and then there's all of this debris

453
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:23,700
that's coming off of the skin

454
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:25,340
because these tumors often have

455
00:17:25,340 --> 00:17:26,820
a tremendous amount of skin.

456
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:29,320
Now, cystic teratomas are benign,

457
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:30,120
and that's a good thing

458
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:32,800
because it's the most common germ cell tumor

459
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:33,540
in a female.

460
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:36,320
However, whenever we have a cystic teratoma,

461
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:38,120
we need to exclude two things

462
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:40,200
to ensure that the tumor is actually benign.

463
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:42,160
The first thing that we need to exclude

464
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:44,040
is the presence of immature tissue.

465
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:46,620
If there's immature tissue in the teratoma,

466
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:48,940
it then becomes an immature teratoma

467
00:17:48,940 --> 00:17:50,760
instead of a mature teratoma,

468
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:54,840
and then it would potentially have malignant potential.

469
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:57,720
It has the ability to spread outside of the region.

470
00:17:58,060 --> 00:17:59,720
So that would be something to worry about.

471
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:02,900
One question that likes to show up on examinations

472
00:18:02,900 --> 00:18:05,860
is what's the most common type of tissue

473
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:08,440
that's immature in an immature teratoma,

474
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:10,600
and the answer is neural ectoderm.

475
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:14,460
So often, immature teratomas contain neural ectoderm,

476
00:18:14,720 --> 00:18:17,140
which then indicates that they're an immature teratoma.

477
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:20,820
Another possibility that could occur within a teratoma

478
00:18:20,820 --> 00:18:23,900
is that the tissue of the teratoma

479
00:18:23,900 --> 00:18:25,620
actually has a cancer.

480
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:28,400
Now, you know that a teratoma contains all mature tissue,

481
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:31,120
like mature skin, mature gut, mature bone, et cetera.

482
00:18:31,660 --> 00:18:34,440
It is possible that the tissue in the teratoma

483
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:35,760
can actually have a cancer.

484
00:18:35,900 --> 00:18:38,620
For example, in the skin of the teratoma,

485
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:40,580
you can have a squamous cell carcinoma,

486
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:42,800
and that's called a somatic malignancy.

487
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:46,000
And, of course, that would also have malignant potential

488
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,740
and could potentially spread in the patient,

489
00:18:48,100 --> 00:18:51,120
and so that would also raise a concern for us,

490
00:18:51,120 --> 00:18:54,520
and we would no longer call this a benign teratoma,

491
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:55,520
but instead we would say

492
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:57,940
it's a teratoma with somatic malignancy.

493
00:18:58,300 --> 00:18:59,680
Now, another important question

494
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:00,920
that shows up on examinations,

495
00:19:00,920 --> 00:19:03,880
what's the most common somatic malignancy

496
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:05,320
that arises in a teratoma,

497
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:08,040
and the answer is squamous cell carcinoma

498
00:19:08,040 --> 00:19:10,060
of the skin of the teratoma.

499
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:13,540
One special type of teratoma is called struma ovariae.

500
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:14,860
In this particular case,

501
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:18,120
you have a teratoma that's mostly composed of thyroid tissue,

502
00:19:18,660 --> 00:19:22,180
and so sometimes patients can develop hyperthyroidism

503
00:19:22,180 --> 00:19:24,500
because the teratoma contains thyroid tissue,

504
00:19:24,600 --> 00:19:26,620
and the thyroid tissue is hyperfunctioning.

505
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:28,280
So let's say that you've got a woman,

506
00:19:28,280 --> 00:19:29,940
she's about the age of 20,

507
00:19:30,300 --> 00:19:32,700
and they tell you that she's also got hyperthyroidism

508
00:19:32,700 --> 00:19:35,400
along with a mass in the ovary.

509
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:38,540
One of the things to consider would be a teratoma

510
00:19:38,540 --> 00:19:40,320
that's mostly made up of thyroid tissue.

511
00:19:40,440 --> 00:19:42,980
Again, we call that struma ovariae.

512
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:45,840
So that's the first type of germ cell tumor.

513
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:47,260
That is cystic teratoma,

514
00:19:47,580 --> 00:19:49,740
and, of course, that's the most common germ cell tumor.

515
00:19:50,260 --> 00:19:53,060
The next germ cell tumor is called dysgerminoma.

516
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:54,200
Dysgerminoma means bad.

517
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:57,940
German refers to the, in this particular case,

518
00:19:58,020 --> 00:20:00,220
the germ cells, and oma refers to a mass.

519
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:05,640
So it is a mass of a bunch of egg-like cells or germ cells,

520
00:20:05,820 --> 00:20:07,820
and that's why we say here that histologically

521
00:20:07,820 --> 00:20:09,640
it's composed of large cells

522
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:12,400
with clear cytoplasm and central nuclei.

523
00:20:12,660 --> 00:20:14,880
That resembles the oocyte,

524
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:18,360
and this description is that of the oocyte, basically.

525
00:20:18,920 --> 00:20:21,720
Now this is the most common malignant germ cell tumor.

526
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:24,680
Remember that the most common benign germ cell tumor

527
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:26,600
and the most common germ cell tumor overall

528
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:27,820
is a cystic teratoma.

529
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:30,280
So this is the most common malignant germ cell tumor.

530
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:34,000
When we have this tumor in the testicle,

531
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:35,360
it's called a seminoma,

532
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:37,740
and when we do testicular tumors,

533
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:39,560
we'll talk about seminoma in more detail.

534
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:41,440
This tumor has good prognosis,

535
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:43,720
or it responds well to radiotherapy,

536
00:20:44,220 --> 00:20:46,900
and one of the tumor markers that can be increased

537
00:20:46,900 --> 00:20:49,540
with a dysgerminoma is LDH.

538
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:51,080
So that may be seen in the serum.

539
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:52,820
This is what the tumor looks like.

540
00:20:52,860 --> 00:20:54,120
You have these nests of cells,

541
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:57,680
but the nests are all sort of composed of these round cells,

542
00:20:58,220 --> 00:21:01,740
and so this is the classic feature of a dysgerminoma.

543
00:21:02,420 --> 00:21:05,180
The next tumor is called endodermal sinus tumor.

544
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:07,100
The idea here is that you have a tumor

545
00:21:07,100 --> 00:21:08,520
that mimics the yolk sac.

546
00:21:09,140 --> 00:21:11,120
What's important, there's three high yields

547
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:13,600
to be familiar with with the endodermal sinus tumor.

548
00:21:13,760 --> 00:21:16,280
Number one, it's the most common germ cell tumor in kids.

549
00:21:16,280 --> 00:21:19,160
So if you've got a five-year-old girl with an ovarian mass,

550
00:21:19,300 --> 00:21:22,080
you really want to think about the endodermal sinus tumor.

551
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:24,240
Number two, just as the yolk sac,

552
00:21:24,500 --> 00:21:26,260
it produces alpha-fetoprotein,

553
00:21:26,540 --> 00:21:28,400
so that when you have a high alpha-fetoprotein,

554
00:21:28,480 --> 00:21:30,500
you want to think about an endodermal sinus tumor,

555
00:21:30,600 --> 00:21:34,480
especially in a child with an ovarian mass, for example.

556
00:21:34,860 --> 00:21:36,620
And then finally, on histology,

557
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:39,160
we see something called Schiller-Duval bodies.

558
00:21:39,620 --> 00:21:43,820
Now Schiller-Duval bodies are what is classically described

559
00:21:43,820 --> 00:21:46,340
as glomeruloid-like structures.

560
00:21:46,520 --> 00:21:48,760
So they're almost glomerular-like

561
00:21:48,760 --> 00:21:50,660
from the glomerulus of the kidney.

562
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:52,360
And this is what it looks like.

563
00:21:52,580 --> 00:21:54,140
You've got a blood vessel in the center,

564
00:21:54,540 --> 00:21:56,400
and then you've sort of got these cells

565
00:21:56,400 --> 00:21:57,740
all around that blood vessel

566
00:21:57,740 --> 00:21:59,260
that are organizing around it,

567
00:21:59,440 --> 00:22:01,900
and then you've got another layer of cells outside of that.

568
00:22:02,420 --> 00:22:04,500
Sort of like this would be Bowman's capsule,

569
00:22:04,920 --> 00:22:06,520
and then this would be Bowman's space.

570
00:22:07,120 --> 00:22:10,020
And so one of the descriptions of this

571
00:22:10,020 --> 00:22:12,160
and the one they like to show on examinations

572
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:14,200
or give you on examinations is to say that

573
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:18,520
biopsies performed and glomeruloid-like structures are seen.

574
00:22:18,940 --> 00:22:20,020
And so you're not going to think about

575
00:22:20,020 --> 00:22:21,120
some kind of kidney tumor.

576
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:25,160
You're going to think about an endodermal sinus tumor.

577
00:22:25,840 --> 00:22:28,760
And again, these are also known as Schiller-Duval bodies.

578
00:22:29,900 --> 00:22:33,020
The next of the germ cell tumors is called choriocarcinoma.

579
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:34,900
What's choriocarcinoma?

580
00:22:34,900 --> 00:22:38,260
It is a malignant proliferation of placental-like tissue.

581
00:22:38,260 --> 00:22:40,880
Now, basically, what you should remind yourselves

582
00:22:40,880 --> 00:22:42,720
of placental tissue is that normally

583
00:22:42,720 --> 00:22:45,160
when you have placental tissue, you have villi.

584
00:22:45,380 --> 00:22:47,860
This is the functional unit of the placenta.

585
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:48,760
You've got a villus.

586
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:50,120
Of course, there's a blood vessel

587
00:22:50,120 --> 00:22:51,340
that runs through the villus.

588
00:22:51,720 --> 00:22:54,160
And remember that the cells that surround the villus

589
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:56,260
are called cytotrophoblasts.

590
00:22:57,300 --> 00:22:59,160
And another cell that surrounds the villus

591
00:22:59,160 --> 00:23:00,260
is called a syncytiotrophoblasts,

592
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:05,080
where you've got multiple nuclei in a cell, for example.

593
00:23:05,600 --> 00:23:08,240
So trophoblasts, whether they be syncytiotrophoblasts,

594
00:23:08,260 --> 00:23:11,720
or cytotrophoblasts, trophoblasts is the key cell

595
00:23:11,720 --> 00:23:13,120
that surrounds the villus.

596
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:15,840
Now, in a choriocarcinoma, what happens is that you get

597
00:23:15,840 --> 00:23:18,900
a malignant proliferation of these trophoblasts.

598
00:23:19,140 --> 00:23:20,340
There will be no villi.

599
00:23:20,660 --> 00:23:21,380
That's important.

600
00:23:21,940 --> 00:23:23,140
There are no villi.

601
00:23:23,480 --> 00:23:25,360
Instead, you have a malignant proliferation

602
00:23:25,360 --> 00:23:27,340
of just the trophoblasts.

603
00:23:27,600 --> 00:23:29,000
And that's what I've stated here in your book.

604
00:23:29,080 --> 00:23:31,260
It's a tumor composed of trophoblasts,

605
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:34,260
both syncytiotrophoblasts and cytotrophoblasts,

606
00:23:34,340 --> 00:23:36,860
and the villi are absent, so there should be no villi.

607
00:23:36,860 --> 00:23:39,920
Now, classically, this is a small hemorrhagic tumor

608
00:23:39,920 --> 00:23:41,940
that spreads very quickly throughout the body.

609
00:23:42,620 --> 00:23:46,660
The reason that this can spread early through the body,

610
00:23:46,760 --> 00:23:49,580
despite the fact that it's only a small tumor in the ovary,

611
00:23:49,780 --> 00:23:52,440
is because this tumor is genetically programmed

612
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:56,040
to invade blood vessels from the very beginning,

613
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:58,060
from its very inception.

614
00:23:58,480 --> 00:24:00,220
And that's because you're well aware of the fact

615
00:24:00,220 --> 00:24:03,760
that trophoblasts are designed to invade and find blood vessels.

616
00:24:03,760 --> 00:24:06,140
That's sort of their natural genetic program.

617
00:24:06,620 --> 00:24:07,960
And so when you get a tumor of these cells,

618
00:24:08,060 --> 00:24:09,760
they very quickly go into the blood,

619
00:24:10,120 --> 00:24:11,300
they spread through the blood,

620
00:24:11,580 --> 00:24:13,340
and then they spread all over the body.

621
00:24:13,620 --> 00:24:16,160
So this is one of the rare tumors in pathology

622
00:24:16,160 --> 00:24:18,560
where you have a tiny primary in the ovary,

623
00:24:18,800 --> 00:24:21,320
but you've got massive tumor all over the body.

624
00:24:21,860 --> 00:24:23,160
And again, that's because these cells

625
00:24:23,160 --> 00:24:25,240
are genetically programmed to go into the blood.

626
00:24:26,040 --> 00:24:28,140
So that's one important gross description.

627
00:24:28,140 --> 00:24:31,240
Choriocarcinoma will do what trophoblasts normally do.

628
00:24:31,320 --> 00:24:34,160
In particular, remember that the syncytial trophoblasts,

629
00:24:34,200 --> 00:24:35,540
they can produce beta-HCG,

630
00:24:35,900 --> 00:24:38,240
and so these tumors will have a high beta-HCG.

631
00:24:38,660 --> 00:24:43,280
Very important to know that patients with choriocarcinoma

632
00:24:43,280 --> 00:24:45,620
have a poor response to chemotherapy.

633
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:48,900
So choriocarcinoma, when it's a germ cell tumor,

634
00:24:49,220 --> 00:24:51,180
has a poor response to chemotherapy.

635
00:24:51,640 --> 00:24:54,340
And I'm going to touch on this in a little more detail

636
00:24:54,340 --> 00:24:57,960
when we cover the gestational lecture

637
00:24:57,960 --> 00:25:00,320
and talk about the different types

638
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:01,960
of hydotetiform moles.

639
00:25:02,320 --> 00:25:04,060
But I want to just bury away this principle

640
00:25:04,060 --> 00:25:04,940
in the back of your mind.

641
00:25:05,060 --> 00:25:06,880
It's going to come up one more time

642
00:25:06,880 --> 00:25:08,420
at the very end of this chapter.

643
00:25:08,780 --> 00:25:10,440
So I'm going to remind you one more time

644
00:25:10,440 --> 00:25:13,740
that choriocarcinoma, when it's a germ cell tumor,

645
00:25:13,920 --> 00:25:15,960
the germ cell variant of choriocarcinoma,

646
00:25:16,300 --> 00:25:18,800
has a poor response to chemotherapy.

647
00:25:19,620 --> 00:25:21,080
The last of the germ cell tumors

648
00:25:21,080 --> 00:25:22,880
is called embrinal carcinoma.

649
00:25:22,880 --> 00:25:25,420
Now, the idea here is that you have a tumor

650
00:25:25,420 --> 00:25:27,980
with cells that look very primitive,

651
00:25:28,240 --> 00:25:29,620
almost embryo-like,

652
00:25:30,080 --> 00:25:31,920
and that's called embrinal carcinoma.

653
00:25:32,380 --> 00:25:35,400
This tumor is aggressive with early metastasis,

654
00:25:35,520 --> 00:25:36,420
and that kind of makes sense

655
00:25:36,420 --> 00:25:38,640
because the embryo-like cells would,

656
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:39,640
when they're primitive,

657
00:25:39,800 --> 00:25:41,480
they have the ability to move and spread.

658
00:25:41,660 --> 00:25:43,400
That's what primitive cells do,

659
00:25:43,720 --> 00:25:45,620
and so that's exactly what these cells do,

660
00:25:45,680 --> 00:25:47,660
and that's called, again, embrinal carcinoma.

661
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:50,080
The third category of ovarian tumors

662
00:25:50,080 --> 00:25:51,680
are the sex cord stromal tumors,

663
00:25:51,680 --> 00:25:54,240
and these are tumors that resemble

664
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:57,720
the normal sex cord stromal tissue of the ovary,

665
00:25:58,040 --> 00:26:00,420
and remember that we talked about this previously

666
00:26:00,420 --> 00:26:02,120
and said that we've got,

667
00:26:02,280 --> 00:26:04,120
among the sex cord stromal tissues,

668
00:26:04,320 --> 00:26:07,160
we've got granulosa cells and theca cells,

669
00:26:07,600 --> 00:26:10,520
whose role is to support the oocyte.

670
00:26:10,740 --> 00:26:12,020
We've got fibrous tissue,

671
00:26:12,480 --> 00:26:14,080
and then very rarely,

672
00:26:14,320 --> 00:26:16,140
we can also have tumors

673
00:26:16,140 --> 00:26:19,000
that are going to arise from Sertoli cells

674
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:19,840
and Leydig cells,

675
00:26:19,860 --> 00:26:20,940
and we're going to talk about that

676
00:26:20,940 --> 00:26:22,440
in more detail in a moment.

677
00:26:23,600 --> 00:26:24,560
So the first example

678
00:26:24,560 --> 00:26:26,500
would be the granulosa theca cell tumor.

679
00:26:26,840 --> 00:26:29,500
This is a tumor of both granulosa and theca cells.

680
00:26:30,280 --> 00:26:32,080
It often produces estrogen,

681
00:26:32,260 --> 00:26:34,740
and remember that the theca cells produce androgen,

682
00:26:34,880 --> 00:26:35,820
which then gets converted

683
00:26:35,820 --> 00:26:37,760
by the granulosa cells to estrogen.

684
00:26:38,140 --> 00:26:40,320
That's the normal physiology,

685
00:26:40,720 --> 00:26:42,460
and so in this tumor as well,

686
00:26:42,700 --> 00:26:44,800
the granulosa cells are going to produce estrogen,

687
00:26:44,800 --> 00:26:45,600
and that's going to be

688
00:26:45,600 --> 00:26:48,240
the dominant hormone present in the blood.

689
00:26:48,680 --> 00:26:49,640
So patients are going to present

690
00:26:49,640 --> 00:26:51,680
with signs and symptoms of estrogen excess.

691
00:26:52,320 --> 00:26:53,880
Now, granulosa theca cell tumors

692
00:26:53,880 --> 00:26:57,880
can actually develop in infants or children,

693
00:26:58,000 --> 00:26:58,600
young children.

694
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:00,480
They can develop in middle-aged women,

695
00:27:00,560 --> 00:27:02,020
and they can develop in older adults.

696
00:27:02,420 --> 00:27:04,840
If you get a granulosa theca cell tumor

697
00:27:04,840 --> 00:27:07,460
in a young child before puberty,

698
00:27:07,640 --> 00:27:09,040
then the child would present

699
00:27:09,040 --> 00:27:11,020
with signs and symptoms of precocious puberty

700
00:27:11,020 --> 00:27:12,600
or early puberty.

701
00:27:12,600 --> 00:27:14,960
If you got a granulosa theca cell tumor

702
00:27:14,960 --> 00:27:16,940
in a middle-aged adult,

703
00:27:17,060 --> 00:27:17,940
then the woman would present

704
00:27:17,940 --> 00:27:19,280
with heavy menstrual bleeding

705
00:27:19,280 --> 00:27:20,840
or maybe bleeding outside

706
00:27:20,840 --> 00:27:22,560
of the menstrual cycle, for example.

707
00:27:23,080 --> 00:27:24,720
And then if you got this tumor

708
00:27:24,720 --> 00:27:27,000
in an older adult that was postmenopausal,

709
00:27:27,280 --> 00:27:29,000
then they would have abnormal uterine bleeding

710
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:30,320
or postmenopausal bleeding,

711
00:27:30,640 --> 00:27:32,580
and that's because the estrogen from the tumor

712
00:27:32,580 --> 00:27:33,960
is going to hit the endometrium

713
00:27:33,960 --> 00:27:35,700
and cause the endometrium to grow

714
00:27:35,700 --> 00:27:36,680
and grow and grow,

715
00:27:36,960 --> 00:27:38,560
and eventually it would begin to bleed.

716
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:41,700
So that's the granulosa theca cell tumor.

717
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:45,120
Sertoli lidic cell tumor is a tumor

718
00:27:45,120 --> 00:27:47,740
that mimics the sex cord stromal elements

719
00:27:47,740 --> 00:27:48,520
of the testicle.

720
00:27:48,780 --> 00:27:50,160
Remember that when you think about

721
00:27:50,160 --> 00:27:52,180
the sex cord stromal elements of the testicle,

722
00:27:52,280 --> 00:27:54,120
the testicle contains these tubules,

723
00:27:54,720 --> 00:27:56,660
and remember that it's within these tubules

724
00:27:56,660 --> 00:27:59,740
that you have the sperm forming.

725
00:28:00,140 --> 00:28:01,360
And then outside of the tubules

726
00:28:01,360 --> 00:28:02,560
you have these pink cells

727
00:28:02,560 --> 00:28:03,660
that are present on occasion.

728
00:28:03,800 --> 00:28:05,040
Those are called lidic cells,

729
00:28:05,540 --> 00:28:08,120
and these are the sex cord stromal cells

730
00:28:08,120 --> 00:28:09,180
of the testicle.

731
00:28:09,180 --> 00:28:11,240
Now because the ovary and testicle

732
00:28:11,240 --> 00:28:14,180
have similar embryologic origins,

733
00:28:14,700 --> 00:28:17,220
it is possible to get a Sertoli lidic cell tumor

734
00:28:17,220 --> 00:28:18,440
in the ovary.

735
00:28:18,920 --> 00:28:21,060
So the Sertoli cells would form tubules

736
00:28:21,060 --> 00:28:22,100
as I've just described.

737
00:28:22,420 --> 00:28:23,240
The lidic cells,

738
00:28:23,300 --> 00:28:24,400
what's important about them

739
00:28:24,400 --> 00:28:26,760
is that they contain a characteristic crystal,

740
00:28:27,100 --> 00:28:29,260
which is called a Rehnke crystal.

741
00:28:29,680 --> 00:28:32,260
And you do need to be aware of Rehnke crystals

742
00:28:32,260 --> 00:28:33,340
for examinations.

743
00:28:33,460 --> 00:28:34,300
If you've got a tumor

744
00:28:34,300 --> 00:28:36,580
and there's these pink cells

745
00:28:36,580 --> 00:28:37,620
that contain crystals,

746
00:28:37,960 --> 00:28:38,900
then you want to think about

747
00:28:38,900 --> 00:28:40,920
a lidic cell component.

748
00:28:41,320 --> 00:28:42,320
And of course these tumors

749
00:28:42,320 --> 00:28:43,600
are going to produce androgen,

750
00:28:43,800 --> 00:28:45,240
and so women can get hertstuism,

751
00:28:45,420 --> 00:28:49,340
which is hair in a male distribution,

752
00:28:49,560 --> 00:28:49,920
for example,

753
00:28:50,020 --> 00:28:51,240
they may develop facial hair,

754
00:28:51,520 --> 00:28:52,580
or virilization.

755
00:28:52,860 --> 00:28:53,880
That's another possibility

756
00:28:53,880 --> 00:28:55,380
if you've got excess androgen.

757
00:28:56,340 --> 00:28:59,780
The third type of sex cord stromal tumor

758
00:28:59,780 --> 00:29:00,580
is a fibroma.

759
00:29:00,840 --> 00:29:01,960
This is very high yield

760
00:29:01,960 --> 00:29:03,400
for the purposes of board exams.

761
00:29:03,780 --> 00:29:06,280
It's a benign tumor of fibroblasts.

762
00:29:06,740 --> 00:29:08,480
But what's even more important than that

763
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:09,660
is that it's associated

764
00:29:09,660 --> 00:29:11,660
with pleural effusion and ascites

765
00:29:11,660 --> 00:29:12,900
in a subset of patients.

766
00:29:13,380 --> 00:29:14,920
And that is called Meigs syndrome.

767
00:29:15,120 --> 00:29:17,780
So a woman who's got an ovarian tumor

768
00:29:17,780 --> 00:29:20,300
with pleural effusion and ascites,

769
00:29:20,800 --> 00:29:24,000
that entire complex is called Meigs syndrome.

770
00:29:24,660 --> 00:29:26,880
Now this is what an ovarian fibroma looks like.

771
00:29:27,600 --> 00:29:29,300
Basically it's a solid tumor

772
00:29:29,300 --> 00:29:31,620
with all these white bands running through it,

773
00:29:31,640 --> 00:29:34,360
and these white bands represent the fibrosis,

774
00:29:34,560 --> 00:29:37,260
i.e. because we're dealing with a fibroma.

775
00:29:37,680 --> 00:29:39,520
The last of the tumors to involve the ovary

776
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:41,160
would be metastatic tumor

777
00:29:41,160 --> 00:29:42,560
that comes from another site

778
00:29:42,560 --> 00:29:43,940
and then spreads to the ovary.

779
00:29:44,420 --> 00:29:45,680
There are many cancers

780
00:29:45,680 --> 00:29:47,040
that can spread to the ovary.

781
00:29:47,300 --> 00:29:49,580
We're only going to discuss two classic examples.

782
00:29:50,020 --> 00:29:51,660
The first is called the Krukenberg tumor,

783
00:29:51,880 --> 00:29:54,120
and the idea here is that we get

784
00:29:54,120 --> 00:29:56,000
a mucinous carcinoma

785
00:29:56,000 --> 00:29:58,220
from some site outside of the ovary

786
00:29:58,220 --> 00:30:00,560
that then subsequently metastasizes

787
00:30:00,560 --> 00:30:02,260
and spreads to both ovaries

788
00:30:02,260 --> 00:30:04,620
so that both ovaries are then involved

789
00:30:04,620 --> 00:30:06,020
by mucinous carcinoma.

790
00:30:06,640 --> 00:30:09,220
Now the site, the primary site

791
00:30:09,220 --> 00:30:10,540
of this particular tumor

792
00:30:10,540 --> 00:30:13,820
can arise from a couple places.

793
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:16,980
Classically, the most common primary site

794
00:30:16,980 --> 00:30:19,380
would be to have a gastric carcinoma,

795
00:30:19,860 --> 00:30:22,360
in particular the diffuse subtype

796
00:30:22,360 --> 00:30:23,480
of gastric carcinoma.

797
00:30:23,880 --> 00:30:24,860
Now let's remind ourselves

798
00:30:24,860 --> 00:30:26,560
that when we think about gastric carcinoma,

799
00:30:26,640 --> 00:30:28,200
there's actually two subtypes.

800
00:30:28,320 --> 00:30:29,440
There's an intestinal type

801
00:30:29,440 --> 00:30:31,420
and there is a diffuse type.

802
00:30:31,740 --> 00:30:33,380
Remember that in the diffuse type,

803
00:30:33,500 --> 00:30:36,160
the characteristic cell that we would see

804
00:30:36,160 --> 00:30:38,040
would be something called the signet ring cell.

805
00:30:38,420 --> 00:30:40,380
Remember that signet ring cells are cells

806
00:30:40,380 --> 00:30:42,500
that have their nucleus pushed off

807
00:30:42,500 --> 00:30:43,800
to one edge of the cell,

808
00:30:44,220 --> 00:30:46,260
and the reason the nucleus is pushed off

809
00:30:46,260 --> 00:30:49,920
is because the cell is full of mucus,

810
00:30:49,920 --> 00:30:52,300
and the mucus displaces the nucleus.

811
00:30:53,080 --> 00:30:55,120
Now that's the diffuse type of gastric cancer,

812
00:30:55,300 --> 00:30:58,260
and that cancer can spread to both ovaries,

813
00:30:58,380 --> 00:31:00,100
giving the patient something called

814
00:31:00,100 --> 00:31:01,080
a Krukenberg tumor.

815
00:31:01,460 --> 00:31:03,340
It is possible that mucinous carcinomas

816
00:31:03,340 --> 00:31:05,480
from other sites could also spread to the ovary.

817
00:31:05,660 --> 00:31:07,360
They would also be called Krukenberg tumor.

818
00:31:07,780 --> 00:31:11,600
For example, the breast can develop a tumor

819
00:31:11,600 --> 00:31:13,260
that can spread to the ovary,

820
00:31:13,380 --> 00:31:15,160
in particular when the tumor in the breast

821
00:31:15,160 --> 00:31:16,400
has signet ring cells,

822
00:31:16,700 --> 00:31:18,020
for example, as would be seen

823
00:31:18,020 --> 00:31:19,320
with lovular carcinoma.

824
00:31:19,780 --> 00:31:22,400
Another example would be colon cancer,

825
00:31:22,580 --> 00:31:24,380
which could be mucinous

826
00:31:24,380 --> 00:31:26,200
and which could go and spread to both ovaries,

827
00:31:26,520 --> 00:31:28,540
but the classic and the most common example

828
00:31:28,540 --> 00:31:31,880
is the diffuse type of gastric carcinoma.

829
00:31:32,340 --> 00:31:33,540
So that's a Krukenberg tumor.

830
00:31:33,660 --> 00:31:35,480
Now, one important distinction to make,

831
00:31:35,540 --> 00:31:39,100
and that is if you have mucinous tumors of the ovary,

832
00:31:39,180 --> 00:31:40,180
you could ask the question,

833
00:31:40,180 --> 00:31:43,440
is the mucinous tumor a primary tumor,

834
00:31:43,600 --> 00:31:45,060
in which case it would, for example,

835
00:31:45,180 --> 00:31:48,000
be a surface epithelial tumor that is mucinous?

836
00:31:48,180 --> 00:31:50,200
Or is the tumor metastatic?

837
00:31:50,740 --> 00:31:52,640
And one way by which we can make that distinction

838
00:31:52,640 --> 00:31:55,420
is to look at whether the tumor involves both ovaries

839
00:31:55,420 --> 00:31:57,040
or only involves one ovary.

840
00:31:57,200 --> 00:31:59,960
If you have mucinous tumor involving only one ovary,

841
00:32:00,200 --> 00:32:01,260
it's more likely to be

842
00:32:01,260 --> 00:32:04,380
a primary surface epithelial mucinous tumor.

843
00:32:04,760 --> 00:32:07,460
However, if the mucinous tumor involves both ovaries,

844
00:32:07,460 --> 00:32:10,760
then it's more likely to have spread from a foreign site.

845
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:13,460
So that's the summary of the Krukenberg tumor,

846
00:32:13,760 --> 00:32:15,900
and I've discussed the high yields in that summary.

847
00:32:15,900 --> 00:32:19,160
The second type of metastatic involvement of the ovary

848
00:32:19,160 --> 00:32:21,820
can be seen with pseudomyxoma peritoneiae.

849
00:32:22,160 --> 00:32:24,520
Now, pseudomyxoma peritoneiae is a term that's used

850
00:32:24,520 --> 00:32:26,740
to describe an abundant amount of mucin

851
00:32:26,740 --> 00:32:28,440
present within the peritoneum.

852
00:32:28,720 --> 00:32:31,600
Classically, it's also known as jelly belly

853
00:32:31,600 --> 00:32:34,200
because you get all of this mucousy fluid

854
00:32:34,200 --> 00:32:36,180
present within the abdomen.

855
00:32:36,580 --> 00:32:39,800
Now, these patients who have pseudomyxoma peritoneiae,

856
00:32:39,800 --> 00:32:43,520
the primary source, the key tumor that's causing that

857
00:32:43,520 --> 00:32:46,340
is usually a tumor within the appendix.

858
00:32:46,960 --> 00:32:50,700
And classically, it's a mucinous carcinoma of the appendix.

859
00:32:51,100 --> 00:32:53,480
And often, that mucinous carcinoma of the appendix,

860
00:32:53,560 --> 00:32:55,460
as it produces massive amounts of mucus

861
00:32:55,460 --> 00:32:57,580
and creates the pseudomyxoma peritoneiae,

862
00:32:57,880 --> 00:33:00,440
will have also metastasized to the ovary.

863
00:33:00,780 --> 00:33:02,000
And so in this particular case,

864
00:33:02,060 --> 00:33:05,420
the patients have a primary tumor of the appendix,

865
00:33:05,420 --> 00:33:09,260
which then produces abundant mucin within the peritoneum

866
00:33:09,260 --> 00:33:12,380
along with metastatic tumor to the ovaries.

867
00:33:12,700 --> 00:33:14,640
So that's pseudomyxoma peritoneiae.

868
00:33:14,900 --> 00:33:17,800
And that closes off our section on ovarian neoplasia.

